      "0.90 MIP",
      "1.13 MIP",
      "1.41 MIP"
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "RELATIVE efficiency (single-arm events dominate; no absolute normalization). Det A is the clean-M1 reference; B/C/D M1 are noisy so single-plane track yield is inflated \u2014 the 3D-pair metric used here is the noise-robust one.",
      "Per-cell statistics are thin in a 6 ms window (~5 pairs/cell), hence the drift+threshold pooling; the resist SHAPE is robust, individual points are ~15-25% error.",
